<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamauchi Kazutoyo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1545">1545</a>–<a href="/years/1605">1605</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yamauchi Kazutoyo was a Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> and sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> in 1600. As a reward Ieyasu gave him Tosa province, taken from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chosokabe-morichika">Chosokabe Morichika</a>. He arrived in 1601, built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kochi">Kochi</a> Castle and suppressed resistance by former Chosokabe retainers; his descendants ruled the Tosa Domain until 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yamauchi-kazutoyo.jpg" alt="Yamauchi Kazutoyo" width="320" height="698" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yamauchi-Kazutoyo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
